  "worked_solution": "In this example, the variable limit $x$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{x}^{0}\\frac{{t}^{2}+7t+12}{t-2}\\,\\text{d}t=-{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{t}^{2}+7t+12}{t-2}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{x}^{0}\\frac{{t}^{2}+7t+12}{t-2}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{t}^{2}+7t+12}{t-2}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{t}^{2}+7t+12}{t-2}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+12}{x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
